===========================================================================
         Zeus BBS-Bingo  Release Version 1.2  November 25, 1995
===========================================================================

Description
~~~~~~~~~~~
  I have yet to see a good BINGO door available.  This is a conversion of
  an Excelsior! BBS door I did last year... there will probably be quite a
  few more conversions in the near future as I miss some of the games that
  I had running on my E! BBS.

  This script is written specifically for Zeus BBSs.

  The Game does require a good IBM type font set, and it also uses a
  lot of ANSI cursor/color codes.

  The Game is designed directly from my experience playing real
  Bingo. You start the game by selecting what type of game to play:

       Standard ....... Across, Up-Down or Diagonal rows.
       Postage Stamp .. The four corners of the card.
       Small X ........ The four spots around the free space.
       Big L .......... A top or bottom Row and the "B" or "O" column.
       Big X .......... Two complete diagonal rows.
       Cover All ...... Every spot must be covered.

  After you select game type, then you are taken to your card and a display
  board showing the "called" numbers.  Once a number has been called, it will
  be highlighted on this board. You have the option of selecting a different
  card before play begins.  No limit on how many times you can change cards.
  Once you have accepted your card, then the first number is called and if 
  you have it on your card, you mark it by pressing the "M" key and the card
  will be highlighted.  You must then press the "SPACE BAR" to call the next
  number.  A Bingo is declared by pressing the "B" key.  The card will be
  checked for a bingo and the player will be notified of a win or not.

  A player can "Q"uit at anytime during the game but it will still be counted
  as a full play.  A random number of calls is determined before each play as
  to how many numbers will be called before a winner in the hall gets a
  BINGO.  Player will be notified if another person gets the BINGO first.

  Enjoy...


How to Install:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   Follow these steps:

 1> UN-LHA the files into your DOORS: assigned directory. All files will
    be located in a directory called "Bingo".  If you are reading this 
    then you have already unarced the file, so just move the Bingo 
    directory into your Doors: assign.

 2> Use a text editor and edit the file "Bingo.CFG" to include the
    following information:
   
    LINE-1:  The Sysop's ALIAS as returned by Zeus.
    LINE-2:  Max number of Turns per day  (0 = disabled)
    LINE-3:  Max number of Plays per turn (0 = disabled)

   (If max turns/day = 5 and max plays/turn = 10, that will allow the user
    to have 5 turns of 10 cards each.)

 3> Add Bingo to your Doors script as a Zeus script.

    OPTION_x:
      ripreset
      callscript 'Doors:Bingo/Bingo'
      signal MENULOOP


Additional Files Created by game:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
     The first time the game is played, it will create the files:

    "Last.DAT" - Last Month's Top Winner.
    "User.DAT"  - Users data file.


Final Notes:
~~~~~~~~~~~~
     At this time, this is an ANSI Only game.  A straight ASCII player
     will NOT be able to play this game, so install it in an ANSI game
     area of Doors if you have one.

     For more info on this or more doors/utilities for Zeus BBS from
     the United States, give my system a call.

